If a patient has a low-back-pain and the patient does not have a contraindication then every clinician should use an NSAID for the low-back-pain.
If a patient has a painful-musculoskeletal-injury and the patient does not have a contraindication then every clinician should use an NSAID for the painful-musculoskeletal-injury.
If a patient has a dental-pain and the patient does not have a contraindication then every clinician should use an NSAID for the dental-pain.
If a patient has a postoperative-pain and the patient does not have a contraindication then every clinician should use an NSAID for the postoperative-pain.
If a patient has a kidney-stone-pain and the patient does not have a contraindication then every clinician should use an NSAID for the kidney-stone-pain.
If a patient has an episodic-migraine-pain and the patient does not have a contraindication then every clinician should use a triptan-NSAID-or-combination with an as-needed-antiemetic for the episodic-migraine-pain.
